# locke over the corpus's shared atoms, written by phil/corpus from readings/locke/logic: not to be edited
logic	s5
atom	beasts_compound_enlarge	beasts compound and enlarge their ideas that way to any degree
atom	beasts_abstract	the power of abstracting is in beasts
atom	general_ideas_distinguish	the having of general ideas puts a perfect distinction betwixt man and brutes
atom	brutes_attain_general	the faculties of brutes attain to the having of general ideas
atom	observed_signs	we observe footsteps in beasts of making use of general signs for universal ideas
atom	beasts_use_signs	beasts have use of words or any other general signs
atom	words_signs_general_ideas	words are made the signs of general ideas
atom	words_general	words are general
atom	separate_circumstances	the circumstances of time and place and other determining ideas are separated from ideas
atom	ideas_general	ideas are general
atom	represent_many	ideas are capable of representing more individuals than one
atom	conforms_to_abstract	an individual has in it a conformity to the abstract idea
atom	of_that_sort	that individual is of that sort
atom	triangle_requires_pains	forming the general idea of a triangle requires some pains and skill
atom	triangle_more_abstract	the general idea of a triangle is one of the more abstract, comprehensive and difficult ideas
atom	tri_oblique	the general idea of a triangle is oblique
atom	tri_rectangle	the general idea of a triangle is rectangle
atom	tri_equilateral	the general idea of a triangle is equilateral
atom	tri_equicrural	the general idea of a triangle is equicrural
atom	tri_scalene	the general idea of a triangle is scalinon
atom	tri_all_and_none	the general idea of a triangle is all and none of these kinds at once
atom	tri_imperfect	the general idea of a triangle is something imperfect
atom	tri_exists	the general idea of a triangle exists
atom	tri_inconsistent_parts	the general idea of a triangle puts together parts of several different and inconsistent ideas
P1	S1	¬beasts_abstract	kind empirical
P2	S1	general_ideas_distinguish
P3	S1	¬brutes_attain_general	kind empirical
P4	S2	¬observed_signs	kind empirical
P5	S2	¬beasts_use_signs	kind empirical
P6	S2	¬observed_signs → ¬beasts_abstract
P7	S2	¬beasts_use_signs → ¬beasts_abstract
P8	S3	words_signs_general_ideas → words_general	kind conceptual
P9	S3	separate_circumstances → ideas_general	kind conceptual
P10	S4	separate_circumstances → represent_many	kind conceptual
P11	S4	conforms_to_abstract → of_that_sort	kind conceptual
P12	S5	triangle_requires_pains
P13	S5	¬triangle_more_abstract
P14	S5	¬tri_oblique ∧ ¬tri_rectangle ∧ ¬tri_equilateral ∧ ¬tri_equicrural ∧ ¬tri_scalene
P15	S5	tri_all_and_none
P16	S6	tri_imperfect
P17	S6	¬◇tri_exists
P18	S6	tri_inconsistent_parts
